     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;white-space:normal;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Dear all,</span></div><div><span style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;white-space:normal;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> more than a year ago, Linda Haines gave me some R code to fit N-mixture models which uses an analytic expression for the likelihood described in this paper:</span></div><div><span style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;white-space:normal;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;white-space:normal;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Haines, L.M., 2016. Maximum likelihood estimation for N‐mixture models. </span><i style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal\">Biometrics</i><span style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;white-space:normal;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">, </span><i style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal\">72</i><span style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;word-spacing:0px;display:inline;white-space:normal;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">(4), pp.1235-1245.</span><br><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">At that point I was extremely busy with things and simply forgot to follow-up on this. Someday I hope to have this put into unmarked but for now it&#39;s not a huge priority. Nevertheless, this formulation is useful in practice and I thought I should put it up on the unmarked email list now (better late than never!).<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\" dir=\"ltr\"> </div>Please check this out if you&#39;re interested!</div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">regards,</div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">andy</div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><br><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\" dir=\"ltr\">---------- Forwarded message ---------<br>From: <strong class=\"gmail_sendername\" dir=\"auto\">Linda Haines</strong> <span dir=\"auto\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">linda....@uct.ac.za</a>&gt;</span><br>Date: Wed, Dec 20, 2017 at 12:14 PM<br>Subject: programs<br>To: Royle, Andy &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">aro...@usgs.gov</a>&gt;<br></div><br><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">Dear Andy,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">   I am attaching my R programs with functions together with a data file (data.txt) and some necessary explanatory notes. The results I obtain agree with those from unmarked. </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">    ...<br></p></div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><b>  </b></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</div></div></div>\r\n"
